  66: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  67:     """Recolor every target pixel by following the ordered two-column substitution legend.
  68: 
  69:     Input structure
  70:     - A dominant background surrounds one multicolor vertical legend: a connected,
  71:       fully filled two-column block with one color pair per row.
  72:     - Other non-background pixels or objects are the targets; divider or frame
  73:       pixels are ordinary target-side structure that remain unchanged unless their
  74:       color is rewritten by the legend.
  75: 
  76:     Rule
  77:     - Read the legend rows from top to bottom as substitutions from the left
  78:       column color to the right column color.
  79:     - For each non-background pixel outside the legend, scan those rows in order;
  80:       whenever the current color equals the row's left color, replace it with the
  81:       row's right color and keep scanning lower rows.
  82:     - Leave the legend itself and background pixels unchanged.
  83: 
  84:     Key insight
  85:     - The same color may be rewritten multiple times, but only by substitutions
  86:       that appear later in the vertical legend, so the row order is part of the
  87:       symbol instruction.
  88:     """
  89:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  90:     assert g.ndim == 2
  91: 
  92:     bg = get_bg(g)
